{
  "dom_id": "step-e11114",
  "name": "Example: Linear Combinations of Elements From a Bivariate Normal Random Variable",
  "problem": "Let $\\mathbf{X} = [X_1,X_2]^T$ be a bivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\boldsymbol{\\mu}$ and covariance matrix $\\Sigma$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the distribution of $Y = 3X_1 + X_2 .$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $\\mathbf{X} = [X_1, X_2]^T$ is a bivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\boldsymbol{\\mu}$ and covariance matrix $\\Sigma,$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu =[\\begin{aligned}{\\mu }_{1} \\\\ {\\mu }_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2} & {\\sigma }_{12} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{21} & {\\sigma }_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthen the random variable $Y,$ defined as\n\n$$\nY= aX_1 + bX_2\n$$\n\nis a normally distributed random variable for all values of $a$ and $b,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E[Y] & =a{\\mu }_{1}+b{\\mu }_{2}, \\\\ Var[Y] & ={a}^{2}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}+2ab{\\sigma }_{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\mu_1 = 2$ and $\\mu_2 = -1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & =\\text{E}[3{X}_{1}+{X}_{2}] \\\\  & =3\\text{E}[{X}_{1}]+\\text{E}[{X}_{2}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot {\\mu }_{1}+{\\mu }_{2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2+(-1) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we have $\\sigma_1^2 = 4, \\sigma_2^2 = 7,$ and $\\sigma_{12} = \\sigma_{21} = -3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Var[Y] & =Var[3{X}_{1}+{X}_{2}] \\\\  & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 4+{1}^{2}\\cdot 7+2\\cdot 3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =36+7-18 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nY \\sim N(5,25).\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-e11114\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n                 \n                <div class=\"example\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Example:</span> Linear Combinations of Elements From a Bivariate Normal Random Variable</div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"e11114\">?</div>\n                    </div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                        <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjp